      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "RFC: Claws",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds an RFC for **Claws**: versioned starter setup manifests for OpenClaw agents. A Claw can compose skills, plugins, MCP servers, connectors, workspace files, persona files such as `SOUL.md`, heartbeat/crons, schedules, and automations into one inspectable setup flow.\n\n## Motivation\n\nOpenClaw has skills, plugins, compatible bundles, package sources, and hosted feeds, but not a focused way to describe a governed scenario-level starter setup that can be inspected, dry-run planned, applied, updated, disabled, removed, and explained later through provenance.\n\n## Current shape\n\n- Uses `Claw` / `Claws` for the user-facing concept and `claw` for schema/feed/CLI kinds.\n- References RFC 0009 as the feed dependency: feeds provide discovery, curation, approval, block, pin, deprecation, and effective-view resolution.\n- Keeps Claws distinct from packages, plugin-bundled skills, compatible bundles, prior Agent Pack/workspace-template proposals, and whole-agent export/import.\n- States the safety guarantee up front: no silent workspace mutation, no silent automation enablement, and no transitive approval of Claw members.\n- Defines typed entries, `inspect`, dry-run apply plans, provenance JSON shapes, workspace-file safety, automation safety, compatibility/migration, and acceptance criteria.\n- Requires apply provenance to include reference accounting for newly created, preexisting direct, and shared artifacts so `remove` releases only the removing Claw's reference.\n- Does not expose a standalone `claws plan` / `claws feed plan` command in v1; `apply --dry-run --json` emits the non-mutating lifecycle plan.\n- Includes a lifecycle diagram for inspect, dry-run apply, mutating apply, status, update, disable, remove, and rollback.\n- Treats `apply` as the Claw lifecycle verb and `remove` as the Claw-level inverse; artifact install/uninstall remains underneath for package-like entries.\n\n## PR sequencing\n\nInitial OpenClaw validation track:\n\n1. `openclaw/rfcs`: RFC and terminology.\n2. `openclaw/openclaw`: one non-mutating Claws validation lifecycle PR.\n\nFuture OpenClaw mutating series, after maintainer acceptance:\n\n1. Artifact apply, provenance persistence, and reference accounting.\n2. Workspace file and persona apply.\n3. Automation enablement, status, and doctor diagnostics.\n4. Update, remove, rollback, and full mutating lifecycle E2E.\n\nClawHub track, dependent on stable OpenClaw schema/parser fixtures and inspect/apply-plan JSON:\n\n1. Schema ingestion and data model.\n2. Publish validation and authoring docs.\n3. Search, detail, and API surfaces.\n4. Feed export and published E2E.\n\n## Validation\n\nCurrent branch head: `5f94cff3f075a24bf7cf3da3ee967be150cddc23`\n\n```text\n$ git diff --check HEAD^..HEAD\n# no output\n\n$ Select-String -Path rfcs\\0016-claws.md -Pattern \"five OpenClaw|five implementation|validation PRs|seven|openclaw claws plan|openclaw claws feed plan|What minimum provenance record|What does `openclaw claws remove`|read-only plan JSON|plan/apply|first complete OpenClaw|six OpenClaw|clawInstall|installedAt\" -Context 1,1\n# no output\n```\r\n",
